1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,200
What if your Copilot Studio agent

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,000
could be called from any app you build?

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,600
Watch this.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,600
You build a great agent in Copilot Studio.

5
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,000
But it's stuck in a chat box.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
To use it in your product, you need code —

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,200
and secure auth. Let's do both.

8
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:21,000
This is the whole integration.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Create the agent. Call run. Get an answer.

10
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,500
The Microsoft Agent Framework treats it

11
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,000
as a first-class agent.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Here it is running.

13
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
I ask a question — and that's a live call

14
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
to my published Copilot Studio agent,

15
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
over Microsoft's Direct-to-Engine API.

16
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
No mock. No fake data.

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Now the part engineers love.

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
This panel shows the exact call path —

19
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
the Agent Framework method, and the real

20
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
HTTP request to Copilot Studio,

21
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,500
with the live endpoint and conversation ID.

22
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:06,500
Full transparency. No black box.

23
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:09,000
And it's secure by design.

24
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Sign-in is Microsoft Entra ID.

25
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The token is scoped to one permission.

26
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Caller and agent must share the same tenant.

27
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:21,500
Enterprise-ready, out of the box.

28
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:24,500
From no-code agent to production integration —

29
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,000
in one afternoon.

30
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:27,400
Code's in the repo. Follow for more.
